# Meerkat TaskPanel supervisor — generated by `install.sh`.
#
# The poll layer runs every minute (a $0 candidate scan; a worker is woken only
# when a card was claimed). The patrol layer runs every five minutes (escalate
# stale claims; report an unreadable heartbeat; no LLM turn by default).
#
# Load with:  crontab <scheduling>/cron/meerkat-taskpanel.cron
# Logs append to {{LOG}}.
#
# Each line names the ABSOLUTE node that rendered this file — never
# `/usr/bin/env node`, which cron resolves against its own minimal PATH (typically
# `/usr/bin:/bin`, holding no nvm and no Homebrew directory) and which therefore
# exits 127 on any machine whose node lives only there.
#
# The `PATH=` line below is what the same problem needs for everything a tick
# *derives*: the wake glue's `exec claude` resolves the host CLI by name, and so
# does the worker's own process tree. It prepends those directories to cron's
# default rather than replacing it, so a child that asks for `sh` or `git` still
# finds them. `PATH=` is a cron *setting line*: it applies to every line after it.
# Via `crontab <file>` that is just this file; `install.sh --supervisor=enable`
# instead appends the lines inside a managed marker block, so there the PATH also
# reaches any line you add below that block (and is removed with it) — see
# docs/scheduling.md §Anywhere — cron.
#
# The interpreter and the directories are version-pinned: after a node or CLI
# upgrade, run `install.sh --force` to refresh this file and re-run `crontab`.

PATH={{UNIT_PATH_CRON}}

* * * * * {{NODE}} {{SUPERVISOR}} --host {{HOST}} --agent {{AGENT}} --once --log {{LOG}} --state {{STATE}} >/dev/null 2>&1
*/5 * * * * {{NODE}} {{SUPERVISOR}} --host {{HOST}} --agent {{AGENT}} --patrol-only --once --log {{LOG}} --state {{STATE}} >/dev/null 2>&1
